WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.520
I should've been... more careful...

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:12.320
I just wanted to... swim in a real ocean...

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.910
Serval-chan... Are you okay?

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.320
I guess this is where my journey ends...

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.710
Serval-chan!

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.470
Why...

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.330
Why did it have to come to this?

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:17.290
We will now be passing through the mountains.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.920
Looks cold...

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.640
There is a hot spring on the other side.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.380
A hot spring?

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:29.370
It is a place where you can 
take a dip in hot water.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.290
How, how? I'm so excited!

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:36.470
You will also see ice-covered 
trees along the way.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:38.490
Would you like to make a snow hut, as well?

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:40.530
I'll make the hot spring our destination.

00:02:41.830 --> 00:02:43.550
This sounds like fun.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.620
A tour through the snowy mountains!

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.050
Let's go!

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:53.880
Boss? We're stuck again?

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:59.030
I see. Snow is slippery.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.030
Wait one moment.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:22.220
Woo-hoo! We're sliding right along! 
Now we can drive as much as we want.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:32.270
The Snowy Mountains Area is a polar climate.

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.770
The temperature is just high 
enough for ice-covered trees.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:39.490
The majority are coniferous needle-leaved 
trees, which tolerate the cold well.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:44.220
This area also has a large amount of 
precipitation, so there is a lot of snow.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:48.160
I've never seen snow before!
I wanna touch it!

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:50.620
I'd like to, also.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:51.810
Understood.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.220
Brr!

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.530
It's cold. It's so cold!

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.940
How mysterious.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.600
It's pretty, huh?

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.780
What's that white stuff over there?

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.820
Oh, I see it.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.980
That is the source of the spring.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:28.580
The hot water coming from it

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:31.430
goes all the way down to the hot spring 
at the bottom of the mountain.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.500
<i>Hot</i> water?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.640
How can water be hot? I wanna see!

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.710
Let's go take a look.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.070
Snowy Mountain Course

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.640
Everything's covered in white.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:48.750
Are there animals living here, too?

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.270
Yes, the snowy mountains also have animals.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:54.840
Many of them are white, 
which camouflages them in the snow.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.210
They may be difficult to spot.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:02.690
Many of the animals have long fur 
for survival in the cold temperatures.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:06.780
Now that you mention it, I'm kind of cold.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:11.280
And will this weather hold?

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:14.570
We'll be fine! It won't take long 
to check out the hot spring.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.180
I can't wait!

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.440
How did the weather change so quickly? 
I can't see past it.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:31.180
What do we do? Lucky-san froze up, too.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.740
I've never been anywhere this cold before.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.830
I feel like I'm frozen, too.

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.390
Y-Yeah...

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:50.570
Serval-chan, let's make 
that thing he mentioned.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.320
It's done!

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.440
We'll wait out the storm in here.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:10.310
Amazing! How'd you know?

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:13.200
When I squeezed some snow 
earlier, it stuck together.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.620
That's why I thought this might work, too.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:19.230
Kaban-chan, you're so observant.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:23.360
I feel a lot warmer just 
being out of that wind.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.230
Thank goodness.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.500
It's not stopping.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.300
Yeah...

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.040
I can hear it from there.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.750
Yeah. Right there.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.740
Here? Okay, got it.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.880
Please don't eat me!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.050
There's a bunch of them!

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.270
Order: Carnivora
Family: Canidae
Genus: Vulpes

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.270
I'm Silver Fox.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:02.150
Order: Carnivora
Family: Canidae
Genus: Vulpes

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.680
She's Ezo Red Fox.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.620
Hi.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:05.930
We took a peek in here because 
she said she heard something.

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:08.110
Strange thing you've made here.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.080
We were pretty startled, too.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.070
You popped your head in so suddenly...

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:18.160
That's how we foxes hunt our prey.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.090
We listen for prey in the snow.

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:24.010
And once we have a mark, we jump,

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.790
and thrust our faces into the snow.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.220
Nuh-uh. We sense their magnetic field.

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:32.040
There you go talking nonsense again.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:34.890
So, what are you two doing here?

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.830
We were on our way to see the hot spring.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:38.930
That's why you came all the way out here?

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.490
You don't look like animals 
who live in the snow to me.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:44.200
You're right. We're really cold.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:46.570
Underestimating the cold will get you killed.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:48.630
You helpless things...

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.780
Here, hold these.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:55.240
It's so warm. What is this?

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.290
It's nice and warm.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.300
Silver Fox, I want one, too.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.070
Doesn't your fur keep you warm enough?

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:09.790
Home's warmer than this, but you 
brought me all the way out here...

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:14.510
We only came out in this weather 
because you insisted we fix it fast.

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.430
Sounds like you're best friends.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.390
What did you come out for?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:21.770
The equipment we always use 
doesn't seem to be working.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.870
We're on our way to check things out.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.020
Looks like the storm's died down.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:29.530
Shall we be on our way, then?

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:34.070
I like it in here. I want 
to stay and laze around.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:36.340
Seriously, you...

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:44.120
We got to take a break, so that worked out.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.960
That was a pretty interesting thing you made.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:54.050
Where will you two go after 
you see the hot spring?

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.660
We're on our way to the harbor!

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:02.310
We were talking about stopping at a 
"hot spring" at the base of the mountain.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:08.010
That's where we came from. 
We can take you along on the way back.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.190
What an incredible color.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:15.460
It smells strange, too.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:23.330
Something's shooting out of the ground!

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.170
I know what it is!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.790
What is it?

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:32.810
There are waves, and it's warm, 
and you can swim in it...

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.920
This is the ocean!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.390
No, it's not.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:40.360
This isn't the ocean.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.310
Aww!

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.410
It's warm!

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:07.870
Really?

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:10.150
That's because the source is really close.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:14.680
Wait... if I went in this, 
It would feel great, wouldn't it?

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.590
That one's regular old cold water.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:25.720
Serval-chan!

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:29.210
I should've been more careful.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:30.810
Why...

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.770
Why did it have to come to this?

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.730
Enjoy the ocean for me, too, okay?

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.300
Strange girls...

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.660
There's a footbath. You should warm up there.

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:45.230
It feels so nice!

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:50.350
This is amazing! A new experience!

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:55.920
It's great. Are you two going to join us?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.140
We'll use the hot spring later.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:02.090
First, Red Fox, do you have any ideas?

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.720
Something feels strange over there, maybe...

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.030
The extractor?

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:17.670
The fox has keen eyesight and 
a very good sense of smell.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:39.780
St-Félicien Zoo, Christine-oneesan (Canada)

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:25.390
They'll pick up on the sounds of mice 
and other small prey under the snow,

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:33.100
head for the tunnel openings their prey made,

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:39.970
and jump into the snow to catch them.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:45.960
There are two main types of foxes, 
the Arctic fox and the red fox.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:12:09.850
Miyagi Zao Fox Village, Satou-oneesan (Miyagi)

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:49.330
The silver fox is a mutation of the red fox.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:54.830
Foxes are black at birth, and their 
fur will change to red or black,

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:58.570
but silver foxes turn to a 
silvery gray-black mixture.

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:00.720
It's not as if, between red and silver foxes,

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.800
one type is more docile and 
the other stronger or anything.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.890
A fox with docile parents will be docile,

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:10.000
and a fox with stubborn parents will be 
stubborn, the same as with people.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:13.180
Something smells good.

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:20.530
Anyway, we don't have an exact location, 
but we want to go into the mountain...

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:23.420
That's a sacred place.

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:25.190
You cannot enter it.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.550
Aww!

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.100
Aww...

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:32.160
Intriguing. Could this be...

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:35.430
Could this be a chance to find out 
the location of the four gods?

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:38.470
Perhaps we should allow them 
to continue their chase.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.440
Indeed.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:49.990
I thought so. The sulfur jammed it up.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:53.530
It's been a while since I've seen this much.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:57.630
When the sulfur deposits are big, 
there are more Ceruleans too, right?

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.590
Do you have to say such ominous things?

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:18.160
Serval-chan, do you think 
this is another "attraction"?

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:18.900
Huh?

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:30.470
Wow, who knew I'd find a hot 
spring on a Cerulean check?

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:36.670
I-I mean... Ahem.

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:41.600
Judging from yesterday's incident, 
the Ceruleans are stealing Sandstar.

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:45.120
Or rather, I believe they may be eating it.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:48.530
On the off-chance that they eat any Friends,

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:51.930
the skills and traits they received 
from the Sandstar might be lost.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:55.120
They might return to their original 
animal forms, or even be wiped out.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.040
There may be any number of effects.

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:59.350
This is all still in the realm of prediction, but...

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:04.460
I can't let them threaten 
those darling Friends!

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:07.200
I'll do whatever it takes 
to find the cause of this.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.930
Sounds like someone who 
really cares about Friends.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:14.110
I wonder what she's like. 
Where could she be right now?

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:16.480
Mirai-san! Look, look!

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.720
Is this the ocean?!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.630
That's not the ocean!

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:23.510
"Mirai-san"...

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:26.130
That voice...

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:36.590
All right. Mission accomplished.

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:38.890
And the hot spring will 
be back to normal, too.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.390
There's so much!

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.260
The mountain's so close!

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:53.740
The mountain the Sandstar comes from?

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:57.620
There are lots of stories 
about that mountain.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.580
I'd like to see it for myself.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:03.890
Do you know what's happening 
with that mountain, Silver Fox?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:07.920
I haven't been there yet. 
It's in another Area, after all.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.490
Not to mention it's a sacred place.

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:12.840
You need the professor's permission to go in.

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:18.140
Red Fox-san? What is it?

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.280
Those are...

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.070
Aren't those Ceruleans?

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:44.560
A-Are they coming this way?

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:48.160
Th-There are too many to fight. Let's run!

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:51.520
They're too fast. Even if we run, 
they'll overtake us.

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.050
We need to hide, or find a high place.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:58.350
But where? There's nowhere to hide!

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:02.410
What'll we do? What can we do?

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:07.770
I'll never be able to play video 
games again? Disappointing...

00:16:12.770 --> 00:16:14.490
Kaban-chan will take care of it!

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.560
She always comes up with 
good ideas at times like this.

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:20.190
Um...

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.430
Like this?

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:33.010
Yes. Thank you.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.190
Okay, I'll push. Everybody in!

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:45.780
They're almost on us!

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:11.640
We're so fast! We can escape now!

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:15.090
If you lean, you can turn it a little.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.440
Amazing, amazing! Sledding's fun!

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:27.850
Let's stop down there. Red Fox-san, 
Silver Fox-san, can we do it?

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:31.110
Leave it to me. I've honed 
my skill in video games.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.140
Silver Fox, more to the right.

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:34.240
Like this?

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:58.310
Thank goodness. We made it safe and sound.

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:01.370
Let's wait until they're gone before 
we descend the mountain.

00:18:01.370 --> 00:18:04.940
I'll get in touch with the hunters later, too.

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:13.540
We made it...

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:17.120
There's so much hot water.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:19.980
The spring's here, too.

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:35.790
It's working. Yes!

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:39.250
What's this? It looks fun!

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:40.660
It's a video game.

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:42.800
Wow.

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.690
Red Fox, take a bath first.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:49.970
I don't wanna. Let me play one level first.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:52.190
One level first!

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.170
Nice and warm.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:04.080
I was waiting. Thanks for 
bringing the hot water back.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:07.270
Order: Rodentia
Family: Caviidae
Genus: Hydrochoerus

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.630
Hot springs are amazing.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.320
I don't handle the cold well, 
so this was a huge help.

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:15.130
I found out today that I don't 
handle the cold well, either.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.300
Hot springs are the best.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:19.930
Hot springs are the best!

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.000
Can I get out now?

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:25.220
Not until you count to thirty.

00:19:26.670 --> 00:19:29.220
Kaban-chan, aren't you getting in?

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:34.380
Um... Is it okay to go in 
with your clothes on?

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:37.010
I get the sense you should 
take them off first.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.170
What are "clothes"?

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:40.360
Huh?

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.360
You know, these.

00:19:43.690 --> 00:19:46.300
Huh?! They come off?!

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:47.700
Do mine, too?!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.040
This is an incredible discovery!

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:52.590
Huh? Ah, um...

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:57.590
But you're not supposed to undress 
completely in front of people, either...

00:19:58.060 --> 00:20:01.980
Wow. We're so smooth without clothes on.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:04.000
Kaban-chan, take yours off, too!

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:11.310
The water's warmer this way...

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.540
Oh, yeah. You know our sled?

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:20.810
Supposedly there's a really 
big one at the harbor.

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:22.720
Wow! Really?

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.990
They say it can move over the water.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:27.560
Why would anyone want to 
do something so scary?

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:31.430
Do you need a sled to go into the ocean?

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:34.750
Well, no, but... Can you swim?

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.500
Huh? Is the ocean that big?

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:46.900
They also say that the humans 
could move it. Maybe Kaban could.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:49.760
Huh? Really?

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:52.610
I'm even more excited to get to the harbor.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.230
Bye!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:56.660
Thank you!

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.340
Take care!

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.570
Later.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:04.420
Once we're through the mountain pass,
we'll get to the ocean!

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.940
I can't wait to see if there are humans.

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:07.830
Yeah!

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:12.160
First, shall we rest for the night?

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:16.460
There's some lodging in a 
good location nearby today.

00:22:56.040 --> 00:23:00.830
Yes, it was stolen on the same day 
as the most recent eruption!

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:04.710
Oh, that one. It was a 
pretty big one, wasn't it?

00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:08.350
Seems like we'll have a lot of 
new Friends born this year.

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:11.490
When are they born again?

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:14.750
When Sandstar touches an animal, 
they become a Friend.

00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:17.450
The same goes for a thing 
that was once an animal.

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:22.540
Yes! Just between us,
Giant Penguin-san is that type of Friend.

00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:24.590
Really?!

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:25.400
That explains things!

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:29.230
I always thought her bearing 
didn't match her appearance.

00:23:29.230 --> 00:23:32.340
It sort of feels like she has a lot of history.

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:34.970
Was Kaban-san just born this year, too?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:38.500
Oh? Kaban-san also came 
through here, did she?

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.390
It's like we have some kind of connection.

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:43.390
PPP Preview!

00:23:43.390 --> 00:23:46.120
This week, we're learning about wolves.

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:50.310
An alpha male and alpha female pair are 
at the top of the hierarchy in a wolf pack.

00:23:50.310 --> 00:23:52.290
What? That's totally cool!

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:54.460
Wolves are super cool!

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:56.370
Next time: "Lodge."
